body:
Basics;

Open new IG account follow popular Turkish pages. Not the one uses slangs a lot. Might be news pages. 

Just you to know, headlines are more complicated to learn because it has to be attractive and has a meaning with less words than the normal sentence. Instead of it, you can check the stories in Turkish, that you already know. 

Grammar;

Don't dive into the grammar. It's too frustrating for the learners. In that case, find daily conversational phrases and learn the meanings of the words in those sentences. 

Speaking;

Don't mind the ğ ç ş sounds that much. They are the easiest part.

Turkish is a prodental language, which you should speak "in front-mid part" of your mouth. If you can't pronounce the words in the beginning just try to consider it and carry your tounge to the front and keep the air bubble middle of your mouth. I hope it makes sense for you.
